{"uid":"792bcff19fda2b5b","name":"test_b3_exceptions_classify_the_finding_not_incidental_words","fullName":"tests.test_confirmation_downgrade#test_b3_exceptions_classify_the_finding_not_incidental_words","historyId":"48115779523e286b79e97f7c62e8fe5d","time":{"start":1791890028073,"stop":1791890028101,"duration":28},"description":"cure-01-03 (PRD B.3, DoD 2): the always-blocking-exception decision\n    is `always_blocking_exception`, an explicit field review asserts --\n    never a text match on the bare words \"secret\"/\"absent\" incidentally\n    present or absent from `clause`/`evidence`. Three findings, none\n    carrying `reopens`/`regression`:\n\n    * an ORDINARY, unlinked defect whose evidence happens to use the word\n      \"absent\" for something that is not an altogether-missing behaviour\n      (an optional argument being absent) -- downgraded, exactly like any\n      other unlinked finding, because the field is not set;\n    * a genuine exposed-secret finding phrased with no occurrence of the\n      word \"secret\" at all (\"password ... committed in plaintext\") --\n      stays blocking, because review set the field explicitly;\n    * a genuine altogether-absent-behaviour finding phrased with no\n      occurrence of the word \"absent\" at all (\"has not been implemented\n      anywhere\") -- stays blocking, because review set the field\n      explicitly.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>cure-01-03 (PRD B.3, DoD 2): the always-blocking-exception decision<br />\nis <code>always_blocking_exception</code>, an explicit field review asserts --<br />\nnever a text match on the bare words &quot;secret&quot;/&quot;absent&quot; incidentally<br />\npresent or absent from <code>clause</code>/<code>evidence</code>. Three findings, none<br />\ncarrying <code>reopens</code>/<code>regression</code>:</p>\n<pre><code>* an ORDINARY, unlinked defect whose evidence happens to use the word\n  &quot;absent&quot; for something that is not an altogether-missing behaviour\n  (an op